Package: mscc-volume
Version: 1.0.0
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Conflicts: mscc-volume-gui
Replaces: mscc-volume-gui
Maintainer: Multus SDR / MSCC Linux <local@localhost>
Depends: python3, python3-tk, pulseaudio-utils | pipewire-pulse
Recommends: mscc
Homepage: https://local/mscc
Description: MSCC Volume: levels of the digital virtual devices on Raspberry Pi OS
 Window with two sliders: VirtualA (receive audio, sdrcore-recv to WSJT-X)
 and VirtualB (transmit audio, WSJT-X to sdrcore-trans).
 .
 Opening it changes nothing. Save keeps the levels in
 $HOME/.local/mscc/volume-levels.conf (applied by mscc-virtual-audio at
 login or desktop Start); Forget deletes that file.
 .
 Desktop menu: MSCC > MSCC Volume. Command: mscc-volume.
 Run as your normal desktop user (not root).
